   "sub": "What actually happens, and what helps",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "If you have been offered a forest programme and are not sure what to think about it, this is for you."
    },
    {
     "t": "h",
     "text": "You do not have to love it"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Many people don't. Some just don't get it. It can take time to settle into the experience. That is fine."
    },
    {
     "t": "quote",
     "text": "Jayden, 15, did not want to go. The forest looked like exactly the kind of place he had no interest in. Wet, pointless, and cold. The guide said: You do not have to do anything. You can walk behind the group, sit on a log. Then she began the walk. Jayden walked behind the group. About twenty minutes in, he spotted something. A mushroom, bright orange, perfectly formed. He stopped. He looked at it for a while. He didn't say anything. He came back the following week.",
     "by": "A story"
    },
    {
     "t": "h",
     "text": "Here's what actually happens on a forest visit"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "The forest gives you something to pay attention to that is not your own mind. A few hours where nobody is asking you to talk about how you are feeling, and your brain gets a break from itself."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "It sounds simple. It kind of is. But that space adds up."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Most people find they get good at taking shelter in the forest. From their thoughts. From the world. Somewhere along the way, without quite knowing how, something good might happen here."
    },
    {
     "t": "h",
     "text": "What helps you make the most of it"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "You are allowed to be silent. You have permission to be loud and lively. You are allowed to be slow… or fast… quiet… or loud. You are allowed to be you."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Wear warm comfortable clothes. Bring water, snacks, a little mat to sit on. It's a practical, earthy place, but you don't have to be uncomfortable."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "If you are in the middle of a thought or an activity, and someone interrupts your moment, it is okay to say: leave me with this for a bit."
    }
   ]
